  "question": {
    "text": "The mean and variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> observations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> of these observations are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the absolute difference of the remaining two observations is :"
  },
